	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>According to website<STRONG> BritneyAccess.com&nbsp;, Spears' new song</STRONG><FONT face=Verdana color=#3a87c0 size=2>&nbsp;</FONT> "Mona Lisa" is set for a Madonna Special coming up on MTV. Britney will perform it.</P>
<P>Plus <SPAN class=postbody><STRONG>TheShh4Life from Brithey's Egg forum</STRONG> writes :</SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody>"H</SPAN>ey guys, well guess what i heard on the <STRONG>radio hot995</STRONG>. Well it seems to go like this.&nbsp;A few months ago britney played a track Mona Lisa on KissFM. Well this is something major. Well the song she did was actually a song intended for her <STRONG>to perform for a Madonna special coming up on MTV this Fall</STRONG>. Remember when Janet and Metallica had an award show dedicated for them, this was a special song britney co-wrote while on tour when she found out about the gig. Britney liking the song so much changed up some lyrics that were geared toward Madge and kind of sent a controversial message of dethrowning Madonna, but she did it because she loved the song so much and wanted it for herself because she had cowritten it, that Jive decided to cut the song. SO britney being the new reformed bad girl decided to play it. Execs at Jive were not happy and nixed the idea of her plannings of a new album this year. <STRONG>Also the list of the performers so far, for the award ceremony is Britney (of course), Chritina Aguilera, and a special duet with Madonna and Babyface. There have also been host talk of Lenny Kravitz and Missy Elliot. Guys stay tuned because this is gonna be so big. Believe me. And remeber the performance roster may change, but bet Britney will be there."</STRONG></P>
