    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=8">Interviews</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Boy George again...</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><IMG src="http://images.contactmusic.com/images/artist/boygeorgeap.jpg" align=right border=0>Last week we reported an article published by <STRONG>ContactMusic.com</STRONG> about <STRONG>Boy George</STRONG> slamming <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> for embracing <STRONG>Kabbalah</STRONG>.<BR>The controversy started because he talks about it on his book <STRONG>"Straight"</STRONG>, which is published this week by <STRONG>Century</STRONG> at £17.99. Interviewed by <STRONG>The Times</STRONG>, he piles it on. </P>
<P><STRONG>The Times</STRONG> asked <STRONG>Boy George</STRONG> what he think of Madonna. “<STRONG>I’ve always been fascinated by Madonna</STRONG>,” he admits. “As I say in my book, <STRONG>she is fascinating, but fascinating probably for all the wrong reasons</STRONG>. Many years ago, when she brought out her sex book, I was asked by a journalist on <STRONG><EM>Rolling Stone</EM></STRONG>, ‘What do you think is next for <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>?’ and I said, ‘She’s going to have a baby and she’s going to find God.’ It was so predictable.” <BR><BR><STRONG>The Times</STRONG> also asked him if he sees himself in some kind of competition with her? “No. I never have," he says. "I’ve always seen what she does as entirely different from what I do. Her agenda with the gay community was always about, ‘It’s good for me’. It’s ironic that she’s joined an organisation (<STRONG>Kabbalah</STRONG>) that says homosexuality is a disease that can be cured and no one picks her up on it. After making all those millions of dollars out of gay people, pretending to kiss girls, pretending to be a lesbian! I think she’s cynical. I’m not cynical. I think that’s the difference.” </P>
<P>On his volume of memoirs, <STRONG>Boy George</STRONG> also slams <STRONG>his father</STRONG>, <STRONG>Elton John</STRONG> and <STRONG>George Michael</STRONG>.&nbsp;</P>
<P><STRONG>Previous related news:</STRONG></P>
<P><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;<A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=6114" target=_blank>Singer Seeking Attention II - Boy George</A><BR></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
